diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f3ccfb6..6a233cd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -121,3 +121,22 @@ The fixed operator never polls. H2D compares the slot and descriptor nonce. D2H
 Deploy the matching Runtime/AICPU iteration together. New AICPU retains legacy and SmallCopy dispatch; old AICPU does not recognize SDF1. The official source fragment includes `secure_dma_fixed_device.cc`, and the mirrored header is `secure_dma_fixed_protocol.h`.
 
 The fixed suite calls the real exported entry: full slots beyond 64 KiB, tail lengths, repeated H2D/D2H, nonce carry/exhaustion, malformed inputs, absent key binding, Host abort, and page revocation immediately after terminal publication. These are local CPU tests; real STARS scheduling and Host/device DMA visibility require hardware validation. Details are in the [iter-007 report](https://github.com/aiyah-meloken/AscendCCv2-Runtime/blob/iter-007/docs/reports/secure-dma/iter-007.md).
+
+## iter-007-zlj AICPU URMA diagnostic
+
+`UMP1` is a separate, 640-byte diagnostic descriptor handled by the existing `SecureDma` entry.
+It reports availability of 27 URMA symbols in the AICPU process. The default only performs
+process-scope symbol lookup. An explicit request flag additionally permits loading standard URMA
+sonames; loading/closing may run constructors/destructors. The probe balances its own loader reference
+and never directly invokes URMA functions, creates queues, or changes the fixed-copy handshake.
+
+`ms_kernels/secure_dma_v2.cmake` includes `secure_dma_urma_probe.cc`. Include it and the accompanying
+headers when syncing this branch into the online CI platform build. The new code has no URMA header
+or mandatory URMA/libdl link dependency; absent weak loader functions produce a negative report.
+The host tests use a mock loader and verify routing, malformed requests, missing exports and reference
+cleanup, including invocation through the exported operator's attribute path without a key binding.
+
+The standalone Host launcher and CI/target instructions are in the workspace's
+`experiments/jfc_notify/README.md`. It dispatches by name on NPU 0, waits for native stream completion,
+and reads the report once. A successful symbol probe does not establish queue creation, endpoint
+routing, device SEND, or graph replay. Those remain separate experiments.
